{
  "name": "FraudNova lead gate v2 (webhook, Sheets, Telegram)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Lead gate v2: score, dedupe and route every lead\nChecks each incoming lead with FraudNova (IP, email and phone) and sorts it into accept, review or reject before it reaches your CRM. Duplicates are answered without spending credits, every outcome is logged to a Google Sheet, review cases are sent to Telegram, and the form always gets a reply.\n\n### How it works\n1. A POST to the webhook carries `email`, `phone`, `country`, `ip` (falls back to the forwarded IP) and optional `name` and `source`.\n2. The email is looked up in the **Leads** tab; a lead seen in the last 24 hours is answered with `duplicate: true`.\n3. Three FraudNova checks run (3 credits). **Decide** keeps the highest score and collects reasons: proxy, VPN, Tor, disposable, honeypot, VOIP, recent abuse.\n4. Score below 60 is accepted; 60 to 84, or any flag, goes to review; 85 or more, or a disposable, honeypot or Tor flag, is rejected with HTTP 403. A failed check never rejects: the lead is held for review with `check_failed`.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the **FraudNova** community node and create its credential with your API key (https://fraudnova.com/dashboard/api-keys; new accounts get free credits).\n2. Create a Google Sheet with the tabs **Leads**, **Review** and **Rejected**, all with the header row listed in the Outcomes note, and connect Google Sheets.\n3. Connect a Telegram bot. Open **Settings** and paste the sheet id and chat id; set the chat id on **Alert failure** as well.\n4. POST a test lead to the production URL.\n\n### Customization\nChange `review_at`, `reject_at`, `reject_flags` or `dedupe_hours` in Settings. Swap Telegram for Slack or email, or add your CRM node after **Append to Leads**.\n\nWatch the walkthrough:\n@[youtube](VIDEO_ID)",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 1
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
